"Internal Error ()\nciteturn8630view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arXiv/arxiv-docs/46793211923f3e84140efe04524a250a93b2577b/source/help/availability.md\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: Failed to fetch https://raw.githubusercontent.com/arXiv/arxiv-docs/46793211923f3e84140efe04524a250a93b2577b/source/help/availability.md: Cache miss\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhat is the difference between the \"created\", \"registered\" and \"published\" date in the DataCite REST API? (https://support.datacite.org/docs/what-is-the-difference-between-the-created-and-registered-date-in-the-datacite-rest-api)\nciteturn8630view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://support.datacite.org/docs/what-is-the-difference-between-the-created-and-registered-date-in-the-datacite-rest-api\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 46\nL0: For AI agents: the docs index is at https://support.datacite.org/llms.txt. Append .md to any documentation page URL to get its markdown version.\nL1: \nL2: 【0†Jump to Content】\nL3: \nL4: 【1†🏳️ Feedback】【2†Home】【3†All content CC-BY†creativecommons.org】\nL5: \nL6: 【2†Home】【4†Guides】【5†API Reference】\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 【6†🏳️ Feedback】【2†Home】【3†All content CC-BY†creativecommons.org】【7†ℹ️ Contact us!†datacite.readme.io】【8†Log In】\nL11: \nL12: Guides\nL13: \nL14: 【7†ℹ️ Contact us!†datacite.readme.io】【8†Log In】\nL15: What is the difference between the \"created\", \"registered\" and \"published\" date in the DataCite REST API?\nL16: # What is the difference between the \"created\", \"registered\" and \"published\" date in the DataCite REST API?\nL17: \nL18: The 【9†DataCite REST API】 response includes the “registered”, \"created\" and \"published\" date. These are defined as follows:\nL19: \nL20: registered: the date when the DOI was registered in the global handle server (in findable state).\nL21: \nL22: created: the date when the new DOI record is created in the DataCite system.\nL23: > 📘\nL24: >\nL25: > These two dates can be exactly the same. However, if a DOI is created in draft state and then changed to findable at a later date, then the created and registered dates will be different\nL26: \nL27: published: if the DOI metadata includes the dateType \"issued\" then this date will appear in the \"published\" field. If there is no dateType \"issued\" then the \"published\" date will be the publicationYear.\nL28: \nL29: More information about 【10†filtering list responses】\nL30: Please refer to the 【11†DataCite Metadata Schema documentation†schema.datacite.org】 for definitions of the properties in the schema that relate to dates (e.g. dateType and publicationYear).\nL31: \nL32: Updated 3 months ago\nL33: \nL34: * * *\nL35: ### What’s Next\nL36: \nL37:   * 【12†DOI States】\nL38: \nL39: Did this page help you?\nL40: \nL41: Yes\nL42: \nL43: No\nL44: \nL45: Copy Page\n"
